IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cea-types`
IMPORT `cea-dates`
IMPORT `cea-value`
IMPORT `cea-duty`
IMPORT `cea-refunds`
IMPORT `cea-goal`

-- Customs and Excise Act 2018 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the Act's text, the Legislation
-- Act 2019 working day and the calendar (Easter Sunday 5 April 2026; Labour
-- Day 26 October 2026; 1 January 2027 a Friday, 1 January 2028 a Saturday).

§ `Tests`

mat MEANS LIST Date 10 7 2026, Date 25 6 2027

§§ `Working days`

#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 3 4 2026) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 6 4 2026) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT `is a working day` (Date 7 4 2026) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 27 4 2026) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 10 7 2026) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 26 10 2026) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT `is a working day` (Date 24 12 2026) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 4 1 2027) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT `is a working day` (Date 5 1 2027) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 4 1 2028) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT `is a working day` (Date 5 1 2028) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT `is a working day` (Date 5 1 2026) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 2 1 2026) `, Matariki days` mat

§§ `Customs value (Schedule 4)`

unrelated MEANS `Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
GIVEN pct IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Buyer and seller`
holding pct MEANS `Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, pct, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `are related` (holding 5)
#ASSERT NOT `are related` (holding 4.9)
#ASSERT NOT `are related` unrelated
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)

GIVEN parties IS A `Buyer and seller`, clause6 IS A BOOLEAN, restricted IS A BOOLEAN, doubt IS A BOOLEAN
      identical IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      similar IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Transaction facts`
tx parties clause6 restricted doubt identical similar MEANS
    `Transaction facts` OF 10000, restricted, FALSE, FALSE, parties, clause6, (LIST 500, 200), FALSE, (LIST 800, 300), 0, FALSE, 100, TRUE, doubt, identical, similar

#ASSERT `the transaction value of` (tx unrelated FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `the Customs value of` (tx unrelated FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `the Customs value of` (tx (holding 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `the Customs value of` (tx (holding 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE (LIST 9800, 9600) (LIST 9000)) EQUALS 9600
#ASSERT `the Customs value of` (tx unrelated FALSE TRUE FALSE EMPTY (LIST 9900, 9950)) EQUALS 9900
#ASSERT `the Customs value of` (tx unrelated FALSE FALSE TRUE (LIST 9700) EMPTY) EQUALS 9700
-- Carrier media: $1,000 of separately valued data is deducted.
#ASSERT `the transaction value of` (`Transaction facts` OF 5000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, unrelated, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 1000, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY) EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT `the transaction value of` (`Transaction facts` OF 5000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, unrelated, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 1000, FALSE, 200, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY) EQUALS 5000

§§ `Duty and payment (ss 120-124)`

#ASSERT `the duty at` 0.05 `of a value of` 9500 `and` 0 `on each of` 0 `units` EQUALS 475
#ASSERT `the duty at` 0 `of a value of` 9500 `and` 2.5 `on each of` 100 `units` EQUALS 250

GIVEN occasion IS A `Payment occasion`, deferred IS A MAYBE DATE
      payments IS A LIST OF Payment
GIVETH A `Duty facts`
duty occasion deferred payments MEANS `Duty facts` OF occasion, Date 16 10 2026, deferred, payments

#ASSERT `the payment date for` (duty `s 122 on entry or other event` NOTHING EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 16 10 2026
#ASSERT `the payment date for` (duty `s 122 on entry or other event` (JUST (Date 20 11 2026)) EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 20 11 2026
-- 20 working days after Friday 16 October, skipping Labour Day: 16 November.
#ASSERT `the payment date for` (duty `s 124(3) an assessment under s 113` NOTHING EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 16 11 2026
-- 20 working days after Monday 14 December, over 25 December to 4 January:
-- 20 January 2027.
#ASSERT `the payment date for` (`Duty facts` OF `s 124(6) a demand under s 138(3) or s 139(4)`, Date 14 12 2026, NOTHING, EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 20 1 2027

-- s 124(7) (added after the independent pass): an earlier time by notice.
#ASSERT `the payment date for` (`Duty facts` OF `s 124(7) an earlier time required by notice`, Date 30 10 2026, NOTHING, EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 30 10 2026

§§ `Late payment penalties (ss 159-160)`

assessed MEANS `s 124(3) an assessment under s 113`
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty assessed NOTHING EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 15 11 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty assessed NOTHING EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 16 11 2026) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty assessed NOTHING EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 22 11 2026) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty assessed NOTHING EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 23 11 2026) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty assessed NOTHING (LIST Payment OF Date 16 11 2026, 500)) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 30 11 2026) EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty assessed NOTHING (LIST Payment OF Date 16 11 2026, 1000)) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 30 11 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty assessed NOTHING (LIST Payment OF Date 20 11 2026, 1000)) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 30 11 2026) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty `s 122 on entry or other event` NOTHING EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 30 11 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the late payment penalties on duty of` 1000 `, facts` (duty `s 122 on entry or other event` (JUST (Date 20 11 2026)) EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 27 11 2026) EQUALS 50

§§ `Refunds and appeals (ss 142, 143)`

GIVEN applied IS A MAYBE DATE, considered IS A DATE, error IS A BOOLEAN, reason IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Refund facts`
refund applied considered error reason MEANS `Refund facts` OF mat, Date 10 1 2026, applied, considered, error, reason

#ASSERT `the duty must be refunded` (refund NOTHING (Date 10 1 2030) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the duty must be refunded` (refund NOTHING (Date 11 1 2030) TRUE FALSE)
-- Legislation Act 2019 s 55 (added after the independent pass): paid on 16
-- March 2026, the 4 years end on Saturday 16 March 2030, so an application on
-- Monday 18 March 2030 is in time; one on Tuesday 19 March is not.
#ASSERT `the duty must be refunded` (`Refund facts` OF mat, Date 16 3 2026, JUST (Date 18 3 2030), Date 1 6 2031, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the duty must be refunded` (`Refund facts` OF mat, Date 16 3 2026, JUST (Date 19 3 2030), Date 1 6 2031, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the duty must be refunded` (refund (JUST (Date 1 12 2029)) (Date 1 6 2031) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the duty must be refunded` (refund NOTHING (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the duty must be refunded` (refund NOTHING (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the refund on a provisional Customs value, duty paid` 1200 `, duty on the final value` 1000 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the refund on a provisional Customs value, duty paid` 1200 `, duty on the final value` 1300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal a decision notified on` (Date 16 10 2026) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 16 11 2026

§§ `The top-level goal`

#ASSERT `the import position for` (tx unrelated FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY) `, ad valorem rate` 0.05 `, specific rate` 0 `, quantity` 0 `, payment facts` (duty assessed NOTHING EMPTY) `, Matariki days` mat `, as at` (Date 23 11 2026) EQUALS `Import position` OF 9500, 475, Date 16 11 2026, 23.75

§§ `Regression: a Sunday 1 January`

-- 1 January 2023 was a Sunday: Monday 2 and Tuesday 3 January are not working
-- days, and Wednesday 4 January is (Legislation Act 2019 s 13(d); corrected
-- after the Electricity Industry Act independent pass found it).
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 2 1 2023) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 3 1 2023) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT `is a working day` (Date 4 1 2023) `, Matariki days` mat
